---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import MarketingChrome from "../../components/MarketingChrome.astro";

const phoneDisplay = "(501) 413-3386";
const tel = "tel:+15014133386";
const sms = "sms:+15014133386";
---

<Base
  title="Ice Cream Shop Websites, See Your Free Demo | NV Labs"
  description="A free demo website for your ice cream shop with a flavor board, seasonal hours, and party pint orders. Call or text (501) 413-3386 to start."
  image="/og.png"
  robots="index, follow"
>
  <MarketingChrome>
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Ice cream shops and creameries</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">A website for your ice cream shop that keeps up with the flavor board</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Free demo first. Flavor board, seasonal hours, and party pint orders. Call or text to get
        started.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a class="btn btn-accent btn-lg" href={tel}>Call {phoneDisplay}</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href={sms}>Text me</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="flavors-title">
      <h2 id="flavors-title">"What flavors do you have today?"</h2>
      <p>
        You probably hear that question all day. Your website can answer it. I'll build a flavor
        board section that matches what's in your case, with your regular lineup and a spot for this
        week's rotating flavors.
      </p>
      <p>
        Keeping it current is simple. You can update it yourself, or text me the changes and I'll
        handle it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="seasonal-title">
      <h2 id="seasonal-title">Seasonal flavors get their own spotlight</h2>
      <p>
        Pumpkin in the fall, peppermint in winter, fresh fruit in summer. Seasonal flavors are a big
        reason people come back. I'll give them their own section so fans can see what's coming and
        what's leaving soon.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="hours-title">
      <h2 id="hours-title">Hours that change with the weather</h2>
      <p>
        Lots of ice cream shops keep longer hours in summer and shorter ones in winter, or close for
        part of the year. I'll make your current hours the first thing people see, with a note about
        seasonal changes. That way nobody shows up in January expecting summer hours.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="party-title">
      <h2 id="party-title">Party pints and catering</h2>
      <p>
        Birthdays, office parties, school events, weddings. If you sell pints to go, cakes, or bring
        a cart to events, I'll add a page for it with a simple request form. It asks for the date,
        how many people, and which flavors, so you get the details all at once.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="diet-title">
      <h2 id="diet-title">Clear dietary notes</h2>
      <p>
        Parents of kids with allergies and folks who skip dairy check before they head over. If you
        offer dairy-free, vegan, or nut-free options, I'll mark them clearly on the flavor board.
        I'll also add a short line about cross-contact if you'd like, worded the way you want it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="phone-title">
      <h2 id="phone-title">Phone first, because that's how people find you</h2>
      <p>
        Most people looking for ice cream are already out and about. Your site will load fast on a
        phone, show your address and hours right away, and let them call or get directions with one
        tap.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
      <h2 id="faq-title">FAQ</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <div>
          <h3>My flavors change every few days. How do I keep the site current?</h3>
          <p>
            I'll set up the flavor board so it's quick to update. If you'd rather not deal with it,
            text me the new lineup and I'll swap it in.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Can people order party pints or cakes ahead of time?</h3>
          <p>
            Yes. I can add an order request form for pints, cakes, or event service. You confirm each
            one the way you normally do.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>We close for part of the winter. Should the site still be up?</h3>
          <p>
            Definitely. It can show a "closed for the season, back in spring" message, so people
            know you're coming back and don't think you shut down.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="cta-title">
      <h2 id="cta-title">Let's make your flavor board live</h2>
      <p>I'll build the demo first. You look at it, then decide. We work by call and text.</p>
      <a class="phone-big" href={tel}>{phoneDisplay}</a>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a class="btn btn-accent btn-lg" href={tel}>Call</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href={sms}>Text</a>
      </div>
      <a class="back-home" href="/">Back to NV Labs home</a>
    </section>
  </MarketingChrome>
</Base>
